---Capacity commitment is a way to purchase compute capacity for BigQuery jobs (in the form of slots) with some committed period of usage. Annual commitments renew by default. Commitments can be removed after their commitment end time passes. In order to remove annual commitment, its plan needs to be changed to monthly or flex first. A capacity commitment resource exists as a child resource of the admin project.
---@class gcp.bigqueryreservation_v1.CapacityCommitment
---@field state? gcp.bigqueryreservation_v1.CapacityCommitmentStateEnum Output only. State of the commitment.
---@field slotCount? string Optional. Number of slots in this commitment.
---@field plan? gcp.bigqueryreservation_v1.CapacityCommitmentPlanEnum Optional. Capacity commitment commitment plan.
---@field renewalPlan? gcp.bigqueryreservation_v1.CapacityCommitmentRenewalPlanEnum Optional. The plan this capacity commitment is converted to after commitment_end_time passes. Once the plan is changed, committed period is extended according to commitment plan. Only applicable for ANNUAL and TRIAL commitments.
---@field failureStatus? gcp.bigqueryreservation_v1.Status Output only. For FAILED commitment plan, provides the reason of failure.
---@field edition? gcp.bigqueryreservation_v1.CapacityCommitmentEditionEnum Optional. Edition of the capacity commitment.
---@field commitmentEndTime? string Output only. The end of the current commitment period. It is applicable only for ACTIVE capacity commitments. Note after renewal, commitment_end_time is the time the renewed commitment expires. So itwould be at a time after commitment_start_time + committed period, because we don't change commitment_start_time ,
---@field multiRegionAuxiliary? boolean Applicable only for commitments located within one of the BigQuery multi-regions (US or EU). If set to true, this commitment is placed in the organization's secondary region which is designated for disaster recovery purposes. If false, this commitment is placed in the organization's default region. NOTE: this is a preview feature. Project must be allow-listed in order to set this field.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the capacity commitment, e.g., `projects/myproject/locations/US/capacityCommitments/123` The commitment_id must only contain lower case alphanumeric characters or dashes. It must start with a letter and must not end with a dash. Its maximum length is 64 characters.
---@field commitmentStartTime? string Output only. The start of the current commitment period. It is applicable only for ACTIVE capacity commitments. Note after the commitment is renewed, commitment_start_time won't be changed. It refers to the start time of the original commitment.
---@field isFlatRate? boolean Output only. If true, the commitment is a flat-rate commitment, otherwise, it's an edition commitment.

---@alias gcp.bigqueryreservation_v1.CapacityCommitmentEditionEnum "EDITION_UNSPECIFIED"|"STANDARD"|"ENTERPRISE"|"ENTERPRISE_PLUS"

